From: TheGammaSqueeze (GammaOS), azahar-nano
Subject: The azahar-nano changes to Azahar 2126.1.2 (core, renderer, dynarmic),
 on 2126.2

GammaOS's 3DS core, azahar-nano, is Azahar 2126.1.2 with about 130 commits of
performance work, most of it measured on the RG DS (a Mali GPU, in-order
Cortex-A55 cores): fastmem and block, dispatch and return stack work in the arm64
JIT, a GPU worker thread that runs the PICA command lists beside the
emulation thread, no GPU wait on a repeated frame, dead work skipping, vertex
and descriptor reuse, faster HLE audio, and more. Most switches default on
for Mali GPUs only, read from Android properties
(persist.gammaos.azahar_nano.<name>); azahar-patch-002 makes that work on
Linux.

Taken from gammaos/emulators/azahar-nano in
https://github.com/TheGammaSqueeze/GammaOSNextDistribution-14 at 8d68e5ecaab
(as cherry-picked into mamaich/GammaOSNext-RG52mini, 94facd34449, whose one
change after it is in src/android), as diff -ruN against the azahar 2126.1.2
tag with its submodules. Left out: src/android (the Android app and the nano
frontend's C interface), GammaOS's gammaos/ folder (build script, profile,
ROM analysis tools), the Android.bp/Android.mk files it renames to *.disabled
and the .github folders.

On the RG52 Mini (Super Mario 3D Land, RetroArch vulkan): full speed (30 fps)
with the CPU capped at 1008 MHz, where 2126.2 with our PGO ran at 24.

Rebased onto 2126.2 (2026-10-28), now a diff -ruN against that tag. Its GDB
and RPC rework changes the run loop and Shutdown that GammaOS rewrote in
src/core/core.cpp, where three hunks failed; those regions are GammaOS's code
with upstream's additions: ProcessPendingWork() on every pass of the run loop,
a debugger's single step through ExecuteCore() where a core runs, and the RPC
server shut down first in Shutdown(). The rest is the same change.

